#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Kursus IBM gratis tentang informasi dan komputasi kuantum"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli operations and observables"
msgstr "Operasi Pauli dan observabel"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore tensoring */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore tensoring */}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Pauli matrices play a central role in the stabilizer formalism.\n"
"We'll begin the lesson with a discussion of Pauli matrices, including some of their basic algebraic properties, and we'll also discuss how Pauli matrices (and tensor products of Pauli matrices) can describe measurements.\n"
msgstr ""
"Matriks Pauli memainkan peran sentral dalam formalisme stabilizer.\n"
"Kita akan memulai pelajaran dengan diskusi tentang matriks Pauli, termasuk beberapa sifat aljabar dasarnya, dan kita juga akan membahas bagaimana matriks Pauli (dan produk tensor dari matriks Pauli) dapat menggambarkan pengukuran.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli operation basics {#pauli-operation-basics}"
msgstr "Dasar-dasar operasi Pauli {#pauli-operation-basics}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here are the Pauli matrices, including the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix and "
"the three non-identity Pauli matrices.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah matriks Pauli, termasuk matriks identitas $2\\times 2$ dan "
"tiga matriks Pauli non-identitas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{I} =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  1 & 0\\\\\n"
"  0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"X =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 1\\\\\n"
"  1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"Y =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & -i\\\\\n"
"  i & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"Z =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  1 & 0\\\\\n"
"  0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{I} =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  1 & 0\\\\\n"
"  0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"X =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 1\\\\\n"
"  1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"Y =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & -i\\\\\n"
"  i & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"Z =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  1 & 0\\\\\n"
"  0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Properties of Pauli matrices {#properties-of-pauli-matrices}"
msgstr "Sifat-sifat matriks Pauli {#properties-of-pauli-matrices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"All four of the Pauli matrices are both unitary and Hermitian.\n"
"We used the names $\\sigma_x,$ $\\sigma_y,$ and $\\sigma_z$ to refer to the non-identity Pauli matrices earlier in the series, but it is conventional to instead use the capital letters $X,$ $Y,$ and $Z$ in the context of error correction.\n"
"This convention was followed in the previous lesson, and we'll continue to do this for the remaining lessons.\n"
msgstr ""
"Keempat matriks Pauli semuanya bersifat uniter dan Hermitian.\n"
"Kita menggunakan nama $\\sigma_x,$ $\\sigma_y,$ dan $\\sigma_z$ untuk merujuk pada matriks Pauli non-identitas sebelumnya dalam seri ini, tetapi lazim menggunakan huruf kapital $X,$ $Y,$ dan $Z$ dalam konteks koreksi kesalahan.\n"
"Konvensi ini diikuti dalam pelajaran sebelumnya, dan kita akan terus melakukannya untuk pelajaran yang tersisa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Different non-identity Pauli matrices *anti-commute* with one another.\n"
msgstr "Matriks Pauli non-identitas yang berbeda *anti-komut* satu sama lain.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"XY = -YX \\qquad XZ = -ZX \\qquad YZ = -ZY\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"XY = -YX \\qquad XZ = -ZX \\qquad YZ = -ZY\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These anti-commutation relations are simple and easy to verify by performing the multiplications, but they're critically important, in the stabilizer formalism and elsewhere.\n"
"As we will see, the minus signs that emerge when the ordering between two different non-identity Pauli matrices is reversed in a matrix product correspond precisely to the detection of errors in the stabilizer formalism.\n"
msgstr ""
"Relasi anti-komutasi ini sederhana dan mudah diverifikasi dengan melakukan perkalian, tetapi sangat penting, dalam formalisme stabilizer dan di tempat lain.\n"
"Seperti yang akan kita lihat, tanda minus yang muncul ketika urutan antara dua matriks Pauli non-identitas yang berbeda dibalik dalam hasil kali matriks bersesuaian tepat dengan deteksi kesalahan dalam formalisme stabilizer.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We also have the multiplication rules listed here.\n"
msgstr "Kita juga memiliki aturan perkalian yang tercantum di sini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"XX = YY = ZZ = \\mathbb{I} \\qquad\n"
"XY = iZ \\qquad YZ = iX \\qquad ZX = iY\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"XX = YY = ZZ = \\mathbb{I} \\qquad\n"
"XY = iZ \\qquad YZ = iX \\qquad ZX = iY\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That is, each Pauli matrix is its own inverse (which is always true for any matrix that is both unitary and Hermitian), and multiplying two different non-identity Pauli matrices together is always $\\pm i$ times the remaining non-identity Pauli matrix.\n"
"In particular, up to a phase factor, $Y$ is equivalent to $X Z,$ which explains our focus on $X$ and $Z$ errors and apparent lack of interest in $Y$ errors in quantum error correction;\n"
"$X$ represents a bit-flip, $Z$ represents a phase-flip, and so (up to a global phase factor) $Y$ represents both of those errors occurring simultaneously on the same qubit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Artinya, setiap matriks Pauli adalah kebalikannya sendiri (yang selalu benar untuk setiap matriks yang bersifat uniter dan Hermitian), dan mengalikan dua matriks Pauli non-identitas yang berbeda selalu menghasilkan $\\pm i$ kali matriks Pauli non-identitas yang tersisa.\n"
"Khususnya, hingga faktor fase, $Y$ setara dengan $X Z,$ yang menjelaskan fokus kita pada kesalahan $X$ dan $Z$ dan tampak kurangnya minat pada kesalahan $Y$ dalam koreksi kesalahan kuantum;\n"
"$X$ merepresentasikan bit-flip, $Z$ merepresentasikan phase-flip, dan sehingga (hingga faktor fase global) $Y$ merepresentasikan kedua kesalahan tersebut yang terjadi secara bersamaan pada qubit yang sama.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Pauli operations on multiple qubits {#pauli-operations-on-multiple-qubits}"
msgstr ""
"Operasi Pauli pada beberapa qubit {#pauli-operations-on-multiple-qubits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The four Pauli matrices all represent operations (which could be errors) on a single qubit — and by tensoring them together we obtain operations on multiple qubits.\n"
"As a point of terminology, when we refer to an *n-qubit Pauli operation*, we mean a tensor product of any $n$ Pauli matrices, such as the examples shown here, for which $n=9.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Keempat matriks Pauli semuanya merepresentasikan operasi (yang bisa berupa kesalahan) pada qubit tunggal — dan dengan mentensor mereka bersama kita mendapatkan operasi pada beberapa qubit.\n"
"Sebagai terminologi, ketika kita merujuk pada *operasi Pauli n-qubit*, kita maksudkan produk tensor dari $n$ matriks Pauli mana pun, seperti contoh yang ditampilkan di sini, untuk $n=9.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X \\otimes X \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X \\otimes Y \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes X \\otimes Y \\otimes Z\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X \\otimes X \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X \\otimes Y \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes X \\otimes Y \\otimes Z\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Often, the term *Pauli operation* refers to a tensor product of Pauli matrices *along with a phase factor,* or sometimes just certain phase factors such as $\\pm 1$ and $\\pm i.$\n"
"There are good reasons to allow for phase factors like this from a mathematical viewpoint — but, to keep things as simple as possible, we'll use the term *Pauli operation* in this course to refer to a tensor product of Pauli matrices without the possibility of a phase factor different than 1.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seringkali, istilah *operasi Pauli* mengacu pada produk tensor dari matriks Pauli *bersama dengan faktor fase,* atau terkadang hanya faktor fase tertentu seperti $\\pm 1$ dan $\\pm i.$\n"
"Ada alasan yang baik untuk mengizinkan faktor fase seperti ini dari sudut pandang matematis — tetapi, untuk menjaga hal-hal sesederhana mungkin, kita akan menggunakan istilah *operasi Pauli* dalam kursus ini untuk merujuk pada produk tensor dari matriks Pauli tanpa kemungkinan faktor fase yang berbeda dari 1.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The *weight* of an $n$-qubit Pauli operation is the number of non-identity Pauli matrices in the tensor product.\n"
"For instance, the first example above has weight $0,$ the second has weight $2,$ and the third has weight $6.$\n"
"Intuitively speaking, the weight of an $n$-qubit Pauli operation is the number of qubits on which it acts non-trivially.\n"
"It's typical that quantum error correcting codes are designed so that they can detect and correct errors represented by Pauli operations so long as their weight isn't too high.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Bobot* dari operasi Pauli $n$-qubit adalah jumlah matriks Pauli non-identitas dalam produk tensor.\n"
"Misalnya, contoh pertama di atas memiliki bobot $0,$ yang kedua memiliki bobot $2,$ dan yang ketiga memiliki bobot $6.$\n"
"Secara intuitif, bobot dari operasi Pauli $n$-qubit adalah jumlah qubit yang menjadi aksinya secara non-trivial.\n"
"Biasanya kode koreksi kesalahan kuantum dirancang sehingga dapat mendeteksi dan mengoreksi kesalahan yang direpresentasikan oleh operasi Pauli selama bobotnya tidak terlalu tinggi.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli operations as generators {#pauli-operations-as-generators}"
msgstr "Operasi Pauli sebagai generator {#pauli-operations-as-generators}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It's sometimes useful to consider collections of Pauli operations as *generators* of sets (more specifically, *groups*) of operations, in an algebraic sense that you may recognize if you're familiar with group theory.\n"
"If you're not familiar with group theory, that's OK — it's not essential for the lesson.\n"
"A familiarity with the basics of group theory is, however, strongly recommended for those interested in exploring quantum error correction in greater depth.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kadang berguna untuk mempertimbangkan kumpulan operasi Pauli sebagai *generator* dari himpunan (lebih spesifik, *grup*) operasi, dalam arti aljabar yang mungkin kamu kenali jika kamu familiar dengan teori grup.\n"
"Jika kamu tidak familiar dengan teori grup, tidak apa-apa — itu tidak penting untuk pelajaran.\n"
"Namun keakraban dengan dasar-dasar teori grup sangat direkomendasikan bagi mereka yang tertarik menjelajahi koreksi kesalahan kuantum lebih dalam.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that $P_1, \\ldots,  P_r$ are $n$-qubit Pauli operations.\n"
"When we refer to the *set generated* by $P_1, \\ldots, P_r,$ we mean the set of *all* matrices that can be obtained by multiplying these matrices together, in any combination and in any order we choose, taking each one as many times as we like.\n"
"The notation used to refer to this set is $\\langle P_1, \\ldots, P_r \\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Misalkan $P_1, \\ldots,  P_r$ adalah operasi Pauli $n$-qubit.\n"
"Ketika kita merujuk pada *himpunan yang dibangkitkan* oleh $P_1, \\ldots, P_r,$ kita maksudkan himpunan *semua* matriks yang dapat diperoleh dengan mengalikan matriks-matriks ini bersama, dalam kombinasi apa pun dan dalam urutan apa pun yang kita pilih, mengambil masing-masing sebanyak yang kita suka.\n"
"Notasi yang digunakan untuk merujuk pada himpunan ini adalah $\\langle P_1, \\ldots, P_r \\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, the set generated by the three non-identity Pauli matrices is "
"as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Misalnya, himpunan yang dibangkitkan oleh tiga matriks Pauli non-identitas "
"adalah sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle X, Y, Z \\rangle = \\bigl\\{\\alpha P\\,:\\,\\alpha\\in\\{1,i,-1,-i\\},\\; P\\in\\{\\mathbb{I},X,Y,Z\\} \\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle X, Y, Z \\rangle = \\bigl\\{\\alpha P\\,:\\,\\alpha\\in\\{1,i,-1,-i\\},\\; P\\in\\{\\mathbb{I},X,Y,Z\\} \\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This can be reasoned through the multiplication rules listed earlier.\n"
"There are 16 different matrices in this set, which is commonly called the *Pauli group*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini dapat ditelusuri melalui aturan perkalian yang terdaftar sebelumnya.\n"
"Ada 16 matriks berbeda dalam himpunan ini, yang umumnya disebut *grup Pauli*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a second example, if we remove $Y,$ we obtain half of the Pauli group.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai contoh kedua, jika kita menghapus $Y,$ kita mendapatkan setengah "
"dari grup Pauli.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle X, Z\\rangle = \\{ \\mathbb{I}, X, Z, -iY, -\\mathbb{I}, -X, -Z, iY \\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle X, Z\\rangle = \\{ \\mathbb{I}, X, Z, -iY, -\\mathbb{I}, -X, -Z, iY \\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here's one final example (for now), where this time we have $n=2.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah satu contoh terakhir (untuk saat ini), di mana kali ini kita "
"memiliki $n=2.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle X \\otimes X, Z \\otimes Z\\rangle = \\{ \\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}, X\\otimes X, Z\\otimes Z, -Y\\otimes Y \\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle X \\otimes X, Z \\otimes Z\\rangle = \\{ \\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}, X\\otimes X, Z\\otimes Z, -Y\\otimes Y \\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this case we obtain just four elements, owing to the fact that $X\\otimes"
" X$ and $Z\\otimes Z$ commute:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam kasus ini kita hanya mendapatkan empat elemen, karena fakta bahwa "
"$X\\otimes X$ dan $Z\\otimes Z$ komut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(X\\otimes X)(Z\\otimes Z) & = (XZ) \\otimes (XZ)\\\\\n"
"& = (-ZX)\\otimes (-ZX)\\\\\n"
"& = (ZX)\\otimes (ZX)\\\\\n"
"& = (Z\\otimes Z)(X\\otimes X).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(X\\otimes X)(Z\\otimes Z) & = (XZ) \\otimes (XZ)\\\\\n"
"& = (-ZX)\\otimes (-ZX)\\\\\n"
"& = (ZX)\\otimes (ZX)\\\\\n"
"& = (Z\\otimes Z)(X\\otimes X).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli observables {#pauli-observables}"
msgstr "Observabel Pauli {#pauli-observables}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Pauli matrices, and $n$-qubit Pauli operations more generally, are unitary, and therefore they describe unitary operations on qubits.\n"
"But they're also *Hermitian* matrices, and for this reason they describe *measurements,* as will now be explained.\n"
msgstr ""
"Matriks Pauli, dan operasi Pauli $n$-qubit secara lebih umum, bersifat uniter, dan karenanya menggambarkan operasi uniter pada qubit.\n"
"Tetapi mereka juga merupakan matriks *Hermitian*, dan untuk alasan ini mereka menggambarkan *pengukuran*, seperti yang akan dijelaskan sekarang.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Hermitian matrix observables {#hermitian-matrix-observables}"
msgstr "Observabel matriks Hermitian {#hermitian-matrix-observables}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider first an arbitrary Hermitian matrix $A.$\n"
"When we refer to $A$ as an *observable*, we're associating with $A$ a certain uniquely defined projective measurement.\n"
"In words, the possible outcomes are the distinct eigenvalues of $A,$ and the projections that define the measurement are the ones that project onto the spaces spanned by the corresponding eigenvectors of $A.$\n"
"So, the outcomes for such a measurement happen to be real numbers — but because matrices have only finitely many eigenvalues, there will only be finitely many different measurement outcomes for a given choice of $A.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertimbangkan pertama matriks Hermitian sembarang $A.$\n"
"Ketika kita merujuk pada $A$ sebagai *observabel*, kita mengasosiasikan dengan $A$ sebuah pengukuran proyektif yang terdefinisi secara unik.\n"
"Dengan kata-kata, kemungkinan hasil adalah nilai eigen berbeda dari $A,$ dan proyeksi yang mendefinisikan pengukuran adalah yang memproyeksikan ke ruang yang direntangkan oleh vektor eigen yang bersesuaian dari $A.$\n"
"Jadi, hasil untuk pengukuran semacam itu ternyata adalah bilangan real — tetapi karena matriks hanya memiliki sejumlah terbatas nilai eigen, hanya akan ada sejumlah hasil pengukuran yang berbeda untuk pilihan $A$ yang diberikan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In greater detail, by the spectral theorem, it is possible to write\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara lebih rinci, berdasarkan teorema spektral, dimungkinkan untuk "
"menulis\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"A = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\lambda_k \\Pi_k\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"A = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\lambda_k \\Pi_k\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for *distinct* real number eigenvalues $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_m$ and "
"projections $\\Pi_1,\\ldots,\\Pi_m$ satisfying\n"
msgstr ""
"untuk nilai eigen bilangan real *berbeda* $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_m$ "
"dan proyeksi $\\Pi_1,\\ldots,\\Pi_m$ yang memenuhi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_1 + \\cdots + \\Pi_m = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_1 + \\cdots + \\Pi_m = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Such an expression of a matrix is unique up to the ordering of the eigenvalues.\n"
"Another way to say this is that, if we insist that the eigenvalues are ordered in decreasing value $\\lambda_1 > \\lambda_2 > \\cdots > \\lambda_m,$ then there's only one way to write $A$ in the form above.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ekspresi matriks seperti itu unik hingga pengurutan nilai eigen.\n"
"Cara lain untuk mengatakannya adalah bahwa, jika kita bersikeras bahwa nilai eigen diurutkan dalam nilai yang menurun $\\lambda_1 > \\lambda_2 > \\cdots > \\lambda_m,$ maka hanya ada satu cara untuk menulis $A$ dalam bentuk di atas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Based on this expression, the measurement we associate with the observable "
"$A$ is the projective measurement described by the projections "
"$\\Pi_1,\\ldots,\\Pi_m,$ and the eigenvalues $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_m$"
" are understood to be the measurement outcomes corresponding to these "
"projections.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berdasarkan ekspresi ini, pengukuran yang kita kaitkan dengan observabel $A$"
" adalah pengukuran proyektif yang digambarkan oleh proyeksi "
"$\\Pi_1,\\ldots,\\Pi_m,$ dan nilai eigen $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_m$ "
"dipahami sebagai hasil pengukuran yang bersesuaian dengan proyeksi ini.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Measurements from Pauli operations {#measurements-from-pauli-operations}"
msgstr "Pengukuran dari operasi Pauli {#measurements-from-pauli-operations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's see what measurements of the sort just described look like for Pauli operations, starting with the three non-identity Pauli matrices.\n"
"These matrices have spectral decompositions as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mari kita lihat seperti apa pengukuran dari jenis yang baru saja dijelaskan untuk operasi Pauli, dimulai dengan tiga matriks Pauli non-identitas.\n"
"Matriks-matriks ini memiliki dekomposisi spektral sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"X = \\vert {+} \\rangle\\langle {+} \\vert - \\vert {-} \\rangle\\langle {-} \\vert\\\\\n"
"Y = \\vert {+i} \\rangle\\langle {+i} \\vert - \\vert {-i} \\rangle\\langle {-i} \\vert\\\\\n"
"Z = \\vert {0} \\rangle\\langle {0} \\vert - \\vert {1} \\rangle\\langle {1} \\vert\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"X = \\vert {+} \\rangle\\langle {+} \\vert - \\vert {-} \\rangle\\langle {-} \\vert\\\\\n"
"Y = \\vert {+i} \\rangle\\langle {+i} \\vert - \\vert {-i} \\rangle\\langle {-i} \\vert\\\\\n"
"Z = \\vert {0} \\rangle\\langle {0} \\vert - \\vert {1} \\rangle\\langle {1} \\vert\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The measurements defined by $X,$ $Y,$ and $Z,$ viewed as observables, are therefore the projective measurements defined by the following\n"
"sets of projections, respectively.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pengukuran yang didefinisikan oleh $X,$ $Y,$ dan $Z,$ dipandang sebagai "
"observabel, karenanya adalah pengukuran proyektif yang didefinisikan oleh "
"himpunan proyeksi berikut, masing-masing.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"\\bigl\\{\\vert {+} \\rangle\\langle {+} \\vert, \\vert {-} \\rangle\\langle {-} \\vert \\bigr\\} \\\\\n"
"\\bigl\\{\\vert {+i} \\rangle\\langle {+i} \\vert, \\vert {-i} \\rangle\\langle {-i} \\vert\\bigr\\} \\\\\n"
"\\bigl\\{\\vert {0} \\rangle\\langle {0} \\vert, \\vert {1} \\rangle\\langle {1} \\vert\\bigr\\}\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"\\bigl\\{\\vert {+} \\rangle\\langle {+} \\vert, \\vert {-} \\rangle\\langle {-} \\vert \\bigr\\} \\\\\n"
"\\bigl\\{\\vert {+i} \\rangle\\langle {+i} \\vert, \\vert {-i} \\rangle\\langle {-i} \\vert\\bigr\\} \\\\\n"
"\\bigl\\{\\vert {0} \\rangle\\langle {0} \\vert, \\vert {1} \\rangle\\langle {1} \\vert\\bigr\\}\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In all three cases, the two possible measurement outcomes are the eigenvalues $+1$ and $-1.$\n"
"Such measurements are commonly called $X$-measurements, $Y$-measurements, and $Z$-measurements.\n"
"We encountered these measurements in the \"General measurements\" lesson of \"General formulation of quantum information,\"\n"
"where they arose in the context of quantum state tomography.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam ketiga kasus, dua kemungkinan hasil pengukuran adalah nilai eigen $+1$ dan $-1.$\n"
"Pengukuran semacam itu umumnya disebut pengukuran $X$, pengukuran $Y$, dan pengukuran $Z$.\n"
"Kita menemukan pengukuran-pengukuran ini dalam pelajaran \"Pengukuran umum\" dari \"Formulasi umum informasi kuantum,\"\n"
"di mana mereka muncul dalam konteks tomografi keadaan kuantum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Of course, a $Z$-measurement is essentially just a standard basis "
"measurement and an $X$ measurement is a measurement with respect to the "
"plus/minus basis of a qubit — but, as these measurements are described here,"
" we're taking the eigenvalues $+1$ and $-1$ to be the actual measurement "
"outcomes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tentu saja, pengukuran $Z$ pada dasarnya hanyalah pengukuran basis standar "
"dan pengukuran $X$ adalah pengukuran terhadap basis plus/minus dari qubit — "
"tetapi, karena pengukuran-pengukuran ini dijelaskan di sini, kita mengambil "
"nilai eigen $+1$ dan $-1$ sebagai hasil pengukuran yang sebenarnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The same prescription can be followed for Pauli operations on $n\\geq 2$ qubits, though it must be stressed that there will still be just two possible outcomes for the measurements described in this way: $+1$ and $-1,$ which are the only possible eigenvalues of Pauli operations.\n"
"The two corresponding projections will therefore have rank higher than one in this case.\n"
"More precisely, for every non-identity $n$-qubit Pauli operation, the $2^n$ dimensional state space always splits into two subspaces of eigenvectors having equal dimension, so the two projections that define the associated measurement will both have rank $2^{n-1}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Resep yang sama dapat diikuti untuk operasi Pauli pada $n\\geq 2$ qubit, meskipun harus ditekankan bahwa masih hanya akan ada dua kemungkinan hasil untuk pengukuran yang dijelaskan dengan cara ini: $+1$ dan $-1,$ yang merupakan satu-satunya nilai eigen yang mungkin dari operasi Pauli.\n"
"Dua proyeksi yang bersesuaian karenanya akan memiliki peringkat yang lebih tinggi dari satu dalam kasus ini.\n"
"Lebih tepatnya, untuk setiap operasi Pauli $n$-qubit non-identitas, ruang keadaan berdimensi $2^n$ selalu terbagi menjadi dua subruang vektor eigen dengan dimensi yang sama, sehingga dua proyeksi yang mendefinisikan pengukuran yang terkait keduanya akan memiliki peringkat $2^{n-1}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The measurement described by an $n$-qubit Pauli operation, considered as an observable, is therefore not the same thing as a measurement with respect to an *orthonormal basis* of eigenvectors of that operation, nor is it the same thing as independently measuring each of the corresponding Pauli matrices independently, as observables, on $n$ qubits.\n"
"Both of those alternatives would necessitate $2^n$ possible measurement outcomes, but here we have just the two possible outcomes $+1$ and $-1.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Pengukuran yang digambarkan oleh operasi Pauli $n$-qubit, dipandang sebagai observabel, karenanya bukan hal yang sama dengan pengukuran terhadap *basis ortonormal* dari vektor eigen dari operasi tersebut, juga bukan hal yang sama dengan mengukur masing-masing matriks Pauli yang bersesuaian secara independen, sebagai observabel, pada $n$ qubit.\n"
"Kedua alternatif tersebut akan membutuhkan $2^n$ kemungkinan hasil pengukuran, tetapi di sini kita hanya memiliki dua kemungkinan hasil $+1$ dan $-1.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, consider the 2-qubit Pauli operation $Z\\otimes Z$ as an observable.\n"
"We can effectively take the tensor product of the spectral decompositions to obtain one for the tensor product.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai contoh, pertimbangkan operasi Pauli 2-qubit $Z\\otimes Z$ sebagai observabel.\n"
"Kita dapat secara efektif mengambil produk tensor dari dekomposisi spektral untuk mendapatkan satu untuk produk tensor.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"Z\\otimes Z & = (\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert - \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert) \\otimes (\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert - \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert)\\\\\n"
"& = \\bigl( \\vert 00\\rangle\\langle 00\\vert + \\vert 11\\rangle\\langle 11\\vert \\bigr) - \\bigl( \\vert 01\\rangle\\langle 01\\vert + \\vert 10\\rangle\\langle 10\\vert \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"Z\\otimes Z & = (\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert - \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert) \\otimes (\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert - \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert)\\\\\n"
"& = \\bigl( \\vert 00\\rangle\\langle 00\\vert + \\vert 11\\rangle\\langle 11\\vert \\bigr) - \\bigl( \\vert 01\\rangle\\langle 01\\vert + \\vert 10\\rangle\\langle 10\\vert \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "That is, we have $Z\\otimes Z = \\Pi_0 - \\Pi_1$ for\n"
msgstr "Artinya, kita memiliki $Z\\otimes Z = \\Pi_0 - \\Pi_1$ untuk\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 = \\vert 00\\rangle\\langle 00\\vert + \\vert 11\\rangle\\langle 11\\vert\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\Pi_1 = \\vert 01\\rangle\\langle 01\\vert + \\vert 10\\rangle\\langle 10\\vert,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 = \\vert 00\\rangle\\langle 00\\vert + \\vert 11\\rangle\\langle 11\\vert\n"
"\\quad\\text{dan}\\quad\n"
"\\Pi_1 = \\vert 01\\rangle\\langle 01\\vert + \\vert 10\\rangle\\langle 10\\vert,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"so these are the two projections that define the measurement.\n"
"If, for instance, we were to measure a $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$ Bell state nondestructively using this measurement, then we would be certain to obtain the outcome $+1,$ and the state would be unchanged as a result of the measurement.\n"
"In particular, the state would not collapse to $\\vert 00\\rangle$ or $\\vert 11\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"jadi ini adalah dua proyeksi yang mendefinisikan pengukuran.\n"
"Jika, misalnya, kita ingin mengukur keadaan Bell $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$ secara non-destruktif menggunakan pengukuran ini, maka kita pasti mendapatkan hasil $+1,$ dan keadaan tidak akan berubah sebagai akibat dari pengukuran.\n"
"Khususnya, keadaan tidak akan runtuh ke $\\vert 00\\rangle$ atau $\\vert 11\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Nondestructive implementation through phase estimation {#nondestructive-"
"implementation-through-phase-estimation}"
msgstr ""
"Implementasi non-destruktif melalui estimasi fase {#nondestructive-"
"implementation-through-phase-estimation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For any $n$-qubit Pauli operation, we can perform the measurement associated"
" with that observable nondestructively using phase estimation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk operasi Pauli $n$-qubit mana pun, kita dapat melakukan pengukuran yang"
" terkait dengan observabel tersebut secara non-destruktif menggunakan "
"estimasi fase.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's a circuit based on phase estimation that works for any Pauli matrix $P,$ where the measurement is being performed on the top qubit.\n"
"The outcomes $0$ and $1$ of the standard basis measurement in the circuit correspond to the eigenvalues $+1$ and $-1,$ just like we usually have for phase estimation with one control qubit.\n"
"(Note that the control qubit is on the bottom in this diagram, whereas in the \"Phase estimation and factoring\"\n"
"lesson of \"Fundamentals of quantum algorithms\" the control qubits were drawn on the top.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah circuit berdasarkan estimasi fase yang bekerja untuk matriks Pauli $P$ mana pun, di mana pengukuran dilakukan pada qubit teratas.\n"
"Hasil $0$ dan $1$ dari pengukuran basis standar dalam circuit bersesuaian dengan nilai eigen $+1$ dan $-1,$ seperti yang biasanya kita miliki untuk estimasi fase dengan satu qubit kontrol.\n"
"(Perhatikan bahwa qubit kontrol ada di bagian bawah dalam diagram ini, sedangkan dalam pelajaran \"Estimasi fase dan pemfaktoran\"\n"
"dari \"Dasar-dasar algoritma kuantum\" qubit kontrol digambar di bagian atas.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Circuit for measuring a Pauli observable using phase "
"estimation](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/stabilizer-formalism/phase-estimation-Pauli.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Circuit untuk mengukur observabel Pauli menggunakan estimasi "
"fase](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/stabilizer-formalism/phase-estimation-Pauli.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A similar method works for Pauli operations on multiple qubits.\n"
"For example, the following circuit diagram illustrates a nondestructive measurement of the $3$-qubit Pauli observable $P_2\\otimes P_1\\otimes P_0,$ for any choice of $P_0,P_1,P_2 \\in \\{X,Y,Z\\}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Metode serupa bekerja untuk operasi Pauli pada beberapa qubit.\n"
"Misalnya, diagram circuit berikut mengilustrasikan pengukuran non-destruktif dari observabel Pauli $3$-qubit $P_2\\otimes P_1\\otimes P_0,$ untuk pilihan $P_0,P_1,P_2 \\in \\{X,Y,Z\\}$ mana pun.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Circuit for measuring a 3-qubit Pauli observable using phase "
"estimation](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/stabilizer-formalism/phase-estimation-3-qubit-Pauli.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Circuit untuk mengukur observabel Pauli 3-qubit menggunakan estimasi "
"fase](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/stabilizer-formalism/phase-estimation-3-qubit-Pauli.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This approach generalizes to $n$-qubit Pauli observables, for any $n,$ in the natural way.\n"
"Of course, we only need to include controlled-unitary gates for *non-identity* tensor factors of Pauli observables when implementing such measurements; controlled-identity gates are simply identity gates and can therefore be omitted.\n"
"This means that lower weight Pauli observables require smaller circuits to be implemented through this approach.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pendekatan ini digeneralisasikan ke observabel Pauli $n$-qubit, untuk $n$ mana pun, dengan cara alami.\n"
"Tentu saja, kita hanya perlu menyertakan gate controlled-unitary untuk faktor tensor *non-identitas* dari observabel Pauli saat mengimplementasikan pengukuran semacam itu; gate controlled-identity hanyalah gate identitas dan karenanya dapat dihilangkan.\n"
"Ini berarti observabel Pauli dengan bobot yang lebih rendah memerlukan circuit yang lebih kecil untuk diimplementasikan melalui pendekatan ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that, irrespective of $n,$ these phase-estimation circuits have just a single control qubit, which is consistent with the fact that there are just two possible measurement outcomes for these measurements.\n"
"Using more control qubits wouldn't reveal additional information because these measurements are already perfect using a single control qubit.\n"
"(One way to see this is directly from the general procedure for phase estimation: the assumption $U^2 = \\mathbb{I}$ renders any additional control qubits beyond the first pointless.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa, terlepas dari $n,$ circuit estimasi fase ini hanya memiliki satu qubit kontrol, yang konsisten dengan fakta bahwa hanya ada dua kemungkinan hasil pengukuran untuk pengukuran-pengukuran ini.\n"
"Menggunakan lebih banyak qubit kontrol tidak akan mengungkapkan informasi tambahan karena pengukuran-pengukuran ini sudah sempurna menggunakan satu qubit kontrol.\n"
"(Satu cara untuk melihat ini adalah langsung dari prosedur umum estimasi fase: asumsi $U^2 = \\mathbb{I}$ membuat qubit kontrol tambahan mana pun di luar yang pertama menjadi tidak berguna.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's a specific example, of a nondestructive implementation of a "
"$Z\\otimes Z$ measurement, which is relevant to the description of the 3-bit"
" repetition code as a stabilizer code that we'll see shortly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah contoh spesifik, dari implementasi non-destruktif dari "
"pengukuran $Z\\otimes Z$, yang relevan dengan deskripsi kode repetisi 3-bit "
"sebagai kode stabilizer yang akan kita lihat segera.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Circuit for measuring a ZZ observable using phase "
"estimation](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/stabilizer-formalism/phase-estimation-ZZ.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Circuit untuk mengukur observabel ZZ menggunakan estimasi "
"fase](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/stabilizer-formalism/phase-estimation-ZZ.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this case, and for tensor products of more than two $Z$ observables more "
"generally, the circuit can be simplified.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam kasus ini, dan untuk produk tensor dari lebih dari dua observabel $Z$ "
"secara lebih umum, circuit dapat disederhanakan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Simplified circuit for measuring a ZZ "
"observable](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/stabilizer-formalism/simplified-ZZ.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Circuit yang disederhanakan untuk mengukur observabel "
"ZZ](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/stabilizer-formalism/simplified-ZZ.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Thus, this measurement is equivalent to nondestructively measuring the "
"parity (or XOR) of the standard basis states of two qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jadi, pengukuran ini setara dengan mengukur secara non-destruktif paritas "
"(atau XOR) dari keadaan basis standar dari dua qubit.\n"
